5. Element and a second homeserver
----------------------------------

Element Web signed in to the lab server through the well-known
discovery, set up cross-signing and key backup, and created a public
room and an encrypted room. An account on another homeserver joined
both. Messages, typing indicators, read receipts and
images were exchanged in both directions, and the encrypted messages
decrypted on both sides.

Counted from the server's logs afterwards:

